92186404474] [:db/retract 17592186404476 :answer-field/choices 17592186404480] [:db/retract 17592186404476 :answer-field/choices 17592186404481] [:db/retract 17592186404476 :answer-field/choices 17592186404477] [:db/retract 17592186404476 :answer-field/choices 17592186404478] [:db/retract 17592186404476 :answer-field/choices 17592186404479] {:db/id 17592186237878 :question/problem "![](images/95/95f7caf5956ab22fe5b47d14098730e23332c41a26d58fc8dc0f0e4ca28546ab.png)\n\nLet $U=\\{l,m,n,o\\}$ be the universal set and let $K=\\{l,m,o\\}.$ What is $\\overset{―}{K}?$" :question/worked-solution "The complement of $K,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{K},$ consists of all the elements in $U$ that are not in $K.$ To represent $\\overset{―}{K},$ we will shade in all the area of $U$ that is *outside* of $K,$ as follows:\n\n![](images/74/74345aeb2a1028e07d155dd357a9bb412860309c99cee37c62380907b3e1bd37.png)\n\nThe element in the shaded area is $n.$ This is the only element of $U$ that is not in $K.$ Therefore, the complement of $K$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{K}=\\{n\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186237670 :answer-field/correct "answer-79ed194c-0f65-59da-943b-f2c0c42ad0b9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4a9cf07e-f5b9-520a-9ad5-197f7e218f70" "answer-64bd11a0-bdcc-5e85-b42d-a6873a171fc8" "answer-39957d77-14fe-5afa-b55e-fc5c5516d904" "answer-514f2e88-12df-5701-b9d7-b5ac210719ae" "answer-79ed194c-0f65-59da-943b-f2c0c42ad0b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a9cf07e-f5b9-520a-9ad5-197f7e218f70" :answer/id #uuid "4a9cf07e-f5b9-520a-9ad5-197f7e218f70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{l,m,n,o\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64bd11a0-bdcc-5e85-b42d-a6873a171fc8" :answer/id #uuid "64bd11a0-bdcc-5e85-b42d-a6873a171fc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{l,m,n\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39957d77-14fe-5afa-b55e-fc5c5516d904" :answer/id #uuid "39957d77-14fe-5afa-b55e-fc5c5516d904" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{m,n\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-514f2e88-12df-5701-b9d7-b5ac210719ae" :answer/id #uuid "514f2e88-12df-5701-b9d7-b5ac210719ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{m\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79ed194c-0f65-59da-943b-f2c0c42ad0b9" :answer/id #uuid "79ed194c-0f65-59da-943b-f2c0c42ad0b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{n\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186240999 :question/problem "If $U=\\{2,4,6,8,…,20\\}$ is the universal set and $B=\\{4,8,12,16,20\\},$ then the complement of $B$ is" :question/worked-solution "The complement of $B,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{B},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $B.$\n\nThe elements of $U$ that are not in $B$ are $2,$ $6,$ $10,$ $14,$ and $18.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $B$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{B}=\\{2,6,10,14,18\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186240345 :answer-field/correct "answer-9a07857f-9b04-5e82-82b2-f3b3a50169ba" :answer-field/choices ["answer-590e2e96-c4ed-5c5c-bd74-ac6935a254f4" "answer-9a07857f-9b04-5e82-82b2-f3b3a50169ba" "answer-30e9f955-9c5f-5995-8b92-02a7c9a66c34" "answer-092d96cc-31d1-57b6-b25f-cb1f645761fb" "answer-dc7d8ee0-c616-5f34-81ae-9932e04e4685"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-590e2e96-c4ed-5c5c-bd74-ac6935a254f4" :answer/id #uuid "590e2e96-c4ed-5c5c-bd74-ac6935a254f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{0,2,6,10,14,18\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a07857f-9b04-5e82-82b2-f3b3a50169ba" :answer/id #uuid "9a07857f-9b04-5e82-82b2-f3b3a50169ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{2,6,10,14,18\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-30e9f955-9c5f-5995-8b92-02a7c9a66c34" :answer/id #uuid "30e9f955-9c5f-5995-8b92-02a7c9a66c34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{2,6,10,14\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-092d96cc-31d1-57b6-b25f-cb1f645761fb" :answer/id #uuid "092d96cc-31d1-57b6-b25f-cb1f645761fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{2,6,10,18\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc7d8ee0-c616-5f34-81ae-9932e04e4685" :answer/id #uuid "dc7d8ee0-c616-5f34-81ae-9932e04e4685" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{6,10,14,18\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186241005 :question/problem "Let $U=\\{a,b,c,…,z\\}$ be the universal set and $Y=\\{a,b,c,…,j\\}$, then $\\overset{―}{Y}=$" :question/worked-solution "The complement of $Y,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{Y},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $Y.$\n\nThe universal set $U$ consists of the letters $a$ through $z,$ while the set $Y$ consists of the letters $a$ through $j.$\n\nSo, the only elements of $U$ that are not in $Y$ are the letters $k$ through $z.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{Y}=\\{k,l,m,…,z\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186240596 :answer-field/correct "answer-7c72eb67-dc8d-5199-baad-e8806a1db03d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3b4fe627-d7c1-50a5-a27e-4f77766ccffc" "answer-1bf1ba90-d97e-56e1-8be0-67555fe8bfec" "answer-7c72eb67-dc8d-5199-baad-e8806a1db03d" "answer-d249a876-1cdc-59b3-9cf5-a76a41e27fb1" "answer-84ffc0a6-3416-5aad-a60b-0475613c9718"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b4fe627-d7c1-50a5-a27e-4f77766ccffc" :answer/id #uuid "3b4fe627-d7c1-50a5-a27e-4f77766ccffc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{i,j,k,…,z\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1bf1ba90-d97e-56e1-8be0-67555fe8bfec" :answer/id #uuid "1bf1ba90-d97e-56e1-8be0-67555fe8bfec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{j,k,l…,z\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c72eb67-dc8d-5199-baad-e8806a1db03d" :answer/id #uuid "7c72eb67-dc8d-5199-baad-e8806a1db03d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{k,l,m,…,z\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d249a876-1cdc-59b3-9cf5-a76a41e27fb1" :answer/id #uuid "d249a876-1cdc-59b3-9cf5-a76a41e27fb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{l,m,n…,z\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84ffc0a6-3416-5aad-a60b-0475613c9718" :answer/id #uuid "84ffc0a6-3416-5aad-a60b-0475613c9718" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{m,n,o…,z\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186399685 :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $x+2y=-8.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x-4.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge -\\frac{1}{2}x-4,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx+2y\\ge -8.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge -8 \\\\ y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186399686 :answer-field/correct "answer-e2fad8bd-39bf-566b-87a3-d1e291f8834c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-55750735-57ef-5704-978f-016957530d23" "answer-2ba7e269-52f8-5419-b3c2-ce59a9e64ef4" "answer-e2fad8bd-39bf-566b-87a3-d1e291f8834c" "answer-510522b1-69d4-55a5-928c-930d7659e841" "answer-9cea3798-a1cb-5294-bc97-fc263be948fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-55750735-57ef-5704-978f-016957530d23" :answer/id #uuid "55750735-57ef-5704-978f-016957530d23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y>-8 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{2}x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ba7e269-52f8-5419-b3c2-ce59a9e64ef4" :answer/id #uuid "2ba7e269-52f8-5419-b3c2-ce59a9e64ef4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge -8 \\\\ y\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2fad8bd-39bf-566b-87a3-d1e291f8834c" :answer/id #uuid "e2fad8bd-39bf-566b-87a3-d1e291f8834c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge -8 \\\\ y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-510522b1-69d4-55a5-928c-930d7659e841" :answer/id #uuid "510522b1-69d4-55a5-928c-930d7659e841" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\le -8 \\\\ y\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9cea3798-a1cb-5294-bc97-fc263be948fc" :answer/id #uuid "9cea3798-a1cb-5294-bc97-fc263be948fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\le -8 \\\\ y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186247383 :question/problem "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{4})=[]+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{4})\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{4}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $6$ and position $4$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe location of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{4})$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{1}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{2}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{3}) \\\\  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{3}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{4}) \\\\  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{2}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{4}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{5}) \\\\  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{2}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{3}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{4}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{5}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{6}) \\\\  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{4})$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So,\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{4})=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3})+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{4})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3}).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186246939 :answer-field/correct "answer-985886cf-1ac8-5f00-a9b7-a6b8dc16ef03" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fb3123f1-385a-5a7b-84da-6fe907b81043" "answer-d35036c1-6254-594b-a400-43e7b6389e44" "answer-985886cf-1ac8-5f00-a9b7-a6b8dc16ef03" "answer-9bce03e9-173f-5fbc-88bd-7c0cb174aeb3" "answer-d3565fb0-5bc7-5c88-a552-65f6218044f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb3123f1-385a-5a7b-84da-6fe907b81043" :answer/id #uuid "fb3123f1-385a-5a7b-84da-6fe907b81043" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d35036c1-6254-594b-a400-43e7b6389e44" :answer/id #uuid "d35036c1-6254-594b-a400-43e7b6389e44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-985886cf-1ac8-5f00-a9b7-a6b8dc16ef03" :answer/id #uuid "985886cf-1ac8-5f00-a9b7-a6b8dc16ef03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9bce03e9-173f-5fbc-88bd-7c0cb174aeb3" :answer/id #uuid "9bce03e9-173f-5fbc-88bd-7c0cb174aeb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3565fb0-5bc7-5c88-a552-65f6218044f8" :answer/id #uuid "d3565fb0-5bc7-5c88-a552-65f6218044f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186253272 :question/worked-solution "First, we define the function $f(x)$ as\n\n$$\nf(x)=(x+2)^{4}(x+5)(x-7).\n$$\n\nSo we're now solving the inequality $f(x)\\ge 0.$\n\nThe solutions to the equation $f(x)=0$ are $x=-5,$ $x=-2,$ and $x=7.$ These roots divide the number line into $4$ subintervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,-5),\\,(-5,-2),\\,(-2,7),\\,(7,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-5)$ | $(-5,-2)$ | $(-2,7)$ | $(7,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $(x+2)^{4}$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x+5$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x-7$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)\\ge 0,$ we look at the bottom row to determine where $f(x)$ is positive.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is positive on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-5)$ and $(7,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, remembering that the roots are also solutions, we conclude that $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in (-\\infty ,-5]\\cup \\{-2\\}\\cup [7,\\infty ).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186252925 :answer-field/correct "answer-54ce1c89-ead7-51f7-8d45-c8b886b66b84" :answer-field/choices ["answer-54ce1c89-ead7-51f7-8d45-c8b886b66b84" "answer-4c47f54b-e89e-5b4f-8218-dda45e7ee776"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54ce1c89-ead7-51f7-8d45-c8b886b66b84" :answer/id #uuid "54ce1c89-ead7-51f7-8d45-c8b886b66b84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-5]\\cup \\{-2\\}\\cup [7,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c47f54b-e89e-5b4f-8218-dda45e7ee776" :answer/id #uuid "4c47f54b-e89e-5b4f-8218-dda45e7ee776" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in \\{-2\\}\\cup [7,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186253275 :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the polynomial on the left-hand side of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4}+3{x}^{3}-28{x}^{2} & ={x}^{2}({x}^{2}+3x-28) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}({x}^{2}+7x-4x-28) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x(x+7)-4(x+7)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x-4)(x+7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we define the function $f(x)$ as\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{2}(x-4)(x+7).\n$$\n\nSo we're now solving the inequality $f(x)\\ge 0.$\n\nThe solutions to the equation $f(x)=0$ are $x=-7,$ $x=0,$ and $x=4.$ These roots divide the number line into $4$ subintervals: \n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,-7),\\,(-7,0),\\,(0,4),\\,(4,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-7)$ | $(-7,0)$ | $(0,4)$ | $(4,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+7$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| ${x}^{2}$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x-4$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)\\ge 0,$ we look at the bottom row to determine where $f(x)$ is positive.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is positive on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-7),$ and $(4,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, remembering that the roots are also solutions, we conclude that $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in (-\\infty ,-7]\\cup \\{0\\}\\cup [4,\\infty ).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186253002 :answer-field/correct "answer-f5cd511b-8452-59e5-b598-ca1eb9dd99c8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-30a52b11-8598-5077-8a15-643c9fad9ec2" "answer-f5cd511b-8452-59e5-b598-ca1eb9dd99c8" "answer-fc70ad66-635a-5913-b502-a590c621334d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-30a52b11-8598-5077-8a15-643c9fad9ec2" :answer/id #uuid "30a52b11-8598-5077-8a15-643c9fad9ec2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-7]\\cup \\{0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5cd511b-8452-59e5-b598-ca1eb9dd99c8" :answer/id #uuid "f5cd511b-8452-59e5-b598-ca1eb9dd99c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-7]\\cup \\{0\\}\\cup [4,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc70ad66-635a-5913-b502-a590c621334d" :answer/id #uuid "fc70ad66-635a-5913-b502-a590c621334d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in \\{0\\}\\cup [4,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186253546 :question/problem "Find all of the subsets of $A=\\{x,y,z\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find every subset of $A,$ we list out every combination of elements within $A.$\n\nWe can use the following diagram to visualize the process:\n\n![](images/1d/1d7c11586a8fff5f63d46d936fd32c7b5fbfc33a406ddf268bfdd934fe787cdf.png)\n\nNote that we must include the empty set since it is a subset of every set.\n\nBy doing this, we get\n\n$$\n∅,\\{x\\},\\{y\\},\\{z\\},\\{x,y\\},\\{x,z\\},\\{y,z\\},\\{x,y,z\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186253065 :answer-field/correct "answer-8dba51cf-7500-588f-9ddc-13c1238ad685" :answer-field/choices ["answer-adaade65-0ace-5c85-9f33-9af310f49494" "answer-73b56506-163b-5f00-81f1-df59bf19d5ac" "answer-6ff14b5d-188a-55a7-affd-519f5a9ab5e3" "answer-8dba51cf-7500-588f-9ddc-13c1238ad685" "answer-6b4a3183-69f6-5f5d-a9e1-c1e072a1f24c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-adaade65-0ace-5c85-9f33-9af310f49494" :answer/id #uuid "adaade65-0ace-5c85-9f33-9af310f49494" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{x\\},\\{y\\},\\{z\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73b56506-163b-5f00-81f1-df59bf19d5ac" :answer/id #uuid "73b56506-163b-5f00-81f1-df59bf19d5ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅,\\{x\\},\\{y\\},\\{z\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ff14b5d-188a-55a7-affd-519f5a9ab5e3" :answer/id #uuid "6ff14b5d-188a-55a7-affd-519f5a9ab5e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅,\\{x\\},\\{y\\},\\{z\\},\\{x,y\\},\\{x,z\\},\\{y,z\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8dba51cf-7500-588f-9ddc-13c1238ad685" :answer/id #uuid "8dba51cf-7500-588f-9ddc-13c1238ad685" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅,\\{x\\},\\{y\\},\\{z\\},\\{x,y\\},\\{x,z\\},\\{y,z\\},\\{x,y,z\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b4a3183-69f6-5f5d-a9e1-c1e072a1f24c" :answer/id #uuid "6b4a3183-69f6-5f5d-a9e1-c1e072a1f24c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅,\\{x\\},\\{y\\},\\{z\\}\\{x,y,z\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186256652 :question/problem "If $X=\\{1,3,5,7\\}$ and $Y=\\{1,2,3,4\\},$ then $Y-X=$" :question/worked-solution "The set $Y-X$ is the set of all elements belonging to $Y$ but *not* $X.$ Note that the elements $1,3\\in X$ are also in $Y,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y-X & =\\{1,2,3,4\\}-\\{1,3,5,7\\} \\\\  & =\\{2,4\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186256038 :answer-field/correct "answer-4d5e7a16-b51c-53c2-b72a-1588ec864b90" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a931d3ce-a37a-5e87-8376-8cdddafbd1e0" "answer-a0801ea7-2e7f-5757-8040-e50f93761a64" "answer-4d5e7a16-b51c-53c2-b72a-1588ec864b90" "answer-29657c78-3578-5c43-b610-e9899615e5fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a931d3ce-a37a-5e87-8376-8cdddafbd1e0" :answer/id #uuid "a931d3ce-a37a-5e87-8376-8cdddafbd1e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{1,2\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0801ea7-2e7f-5757-8040-e50f93761a64" :answer/id #uuid "a0801ea7-2e7f-5757-8040-e50f93761a64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{1,3\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d5e7a16-b51c-53c2-b72a-1588ec864b90" :answer/id #uuid "4d5e7a16-b51c-53c2-b72a-1588ec864b90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{2,4\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29657c78-3578-5c43-b610-e9899615e5fc" :answer/id #uuid "29657c78-3578-5c43-b610-e9899615e5fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{5,7\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186256677 :question/problem "If $C=\\{-3,-1,0,5,10\\}$ and $D=\\{-2,-1,0,1\\}$, then $C∖D=$" :question/worked-solution "The set $C∖D$ is the set of all elements belonging to $C$ but *not* $D.$ Note that the elements $-1,0\\in D$ are also in $C,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C∖D & =C-D \\\\  & =\\{-3,-1,0,5,10\\}-\\{-2,-1,0,1\\} \\\\  & =\\{-3,5,10\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186256119 :answer-field/correct "answer-e222de57-32d1-57f9-b8e5-e327cccbb0a8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e2571f68-6cbd-5767-bbb1-d285a269424b" "answer-bd760fde-6a8f-5d98-9d4c-4d18e213cd8b" "answer-e222de57-32d1-57f9-b8e5-e327cccbb0a8" "answer-cab4fd57-f8a1-5eea-9750-91ba3eea2e75" "answer-2987d072-93a7-5265-bd24-21d4a5023733"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2571f68-6cbd-5767-bbb1-d285a269424b" :answer/id #uuid "e2571f68-6cbd-5767-bbb1-d285a269424b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-2,1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd760fde-6a8f-5d98-9d4c-4d18e213cd8b" :answer/id #uuid "bd760fde-6a8f-5d98-9d4c-4d18e213cd8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-3,1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e222de57-32d1-57f9-b8e5-e327cccbb0a8" :answer/id #uuid "e222de57-32d1-57f9-b8e5-e327cccbb0a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-3,5,10\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cab4fd57-f8a1-5eea-9750-91ba3eea2e75" :answer/id #uuid "cab4fd57-f8a1-5eea-9750-91ba3eea2e75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-3,5\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2987d072-93a7-5265-bd24-21d4a5023733" :answer/id #uuid "2987d072-93a7-5265-bd24-21d4a5023733" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{10\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186262704 :question/worked-solution "First, the vector equation of the line is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3t \\\\ 2t \\\\ 7t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7-3t \\\\ -11+2t \\\\ 3+7t\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Therefore, the parametric equations are:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=7-3t \\\\ y=-11+2t \\\\ z=3+7t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186262258 :answer-field/correct "answer-bddffa79-df45-5156-a1ce-3514e6387fb3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8e7b1f0e-6aee-53a0-9934-d5d64d9aadef" "answer-7b303939-05de-583e-8174-21d10e301064" "answer-cabd9719-aff1-5cd5-b54b-f9260764be67" "answer-bddffa79-df45-5156-a1ce-3514e6387fb3" "answer-df58bcd8-8519-5abd-864a-5386206d78bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e7b1f0e-6aee-53a0-9934-d5d64d9aadef" :answer/id #uuid "8e7b1f0e-6aee-53a0-9934-d5d64d9aadef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=7+3t \\\\ y=-11+2t \\\\ z=3-7t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b303939-05de-583e-8174-21d10e301064" :answer/id #uuid "7b303939-05de-583e-8174-21d10e301064" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=7+3t \\\\ y=11+2t \\\\ z=3-7t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cabd9719-aff1-5cd5-b54b-f9260764be67" :answer/id #uuid "cabd9719-aff1-5cd5-b54b-f9260764be67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=7+3t \\\\ y=11-2t \\\\ z=3+7t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bddffa79-df45-5156-a1ce-3514e6387fb3" :answer/id #uuid "bddffa79-df45-5156-a1ce-3514e6387fb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=7-3t \\\\ y=-11+2t \\\\ z=3+7t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df58bcd8-8519-5abd-864a-5386206d78bc" :answer/id #uuid "df58bcd8-8519-5abd-864a-5386206d78bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=7-3t \\\\ y=-11-2t \\\\ z=4+7t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186262707 :question/worked-solution "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nComparing the above to our given equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-10}{7}=\\frac{y-(-8)}{-4}=\\frac{z-(-1)}{11},\n$$\n\nwe find that our line passes through the point $P(10,-8,-1)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨7,-4,11⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations are the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=10+7t \\\\ y=-8-4t \\\\ z=-1+11t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186262402 :answer-field/correct "answer-49fbf7a6-3fac-5080-8363-be5656606e0c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-020acfa4-543c-54b8-8b22-7b878f6d0d45" "answer-6aeab917-03af-5aaa-807f-606ae765d324" "answer-49fbf7a6-3fac-5080-8363-be5656606e0c" "answer-9256b135-afaa-56c0-87dd-9ef764465aa3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-020acfa4-543c-54b8-8b22-7b878f6d0d45" :answer/id #uuid "020acfa4-543c-54b8-8b22-7b878f6d0d45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=10+7t \\\\ y=-4-8t \\\\ z=-1-11t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6aeab917-03af-5aaa-807f-606ae765d324" :answer/id #uuid "6aeab917-03af-5aaa-807f-606ae765d324" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=10+7t \\\\ y=-7-8t \\\\ z=-1+t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49fbf7a6-3fac-5080-8363-be5656606e0c" :answer/id #uuid "49fbf7a6-3fac-5080-8363-be5656606e0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=10+7t \\\\ y=-8-4t \\\\ z=-1+11t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9256b135-afaa-56c0-87dd-9ef764465aa3" :answer/id #uuid "9256b135-afaa-56c0-87dd-9ef764465aa3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=10+7t \\\\ y=8+4t \\\\ z=-1+11t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186400380 :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix consists of two parts: the coefficient matrix and the column of constants.\n\nThe coefficient matrix represents the coefficients in the linear system, while the column of constants represents the constants on the right-hand sides of the equations.\n\nUsing the variables $x$ and  $y$,  the corresponding system of equations is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}0x+8y=6 \\\\ 4x+y=-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy simplifying, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}8y=6 \\\\ 4x+y=-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186400381 :answer-field/correct "answer-38120e62-d95b-502d-9288-454ec459aba2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-24490954-ab21-5051-9c79-0188676572bd" "answer-38120e62-d95b-502d-9288-454ec459aba2" "answer-ca1fb4a7-0229-50a8-b462-cf1f3e49f409" "answer-b0af48a4-a01a-5ac1-a551-44dbb13e7334" "answer-57c2694f-57f8-54fb-b264-a6f49a025275"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24490954-ab21-5051-9c79-0188676572bd" :answer/id #uuid "24490954-ab21-5051-9c79-0188676572bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}8x+y=6 \\\\ 4x+y=-9\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38120e62-d95b-502d-9288-454ec459aba2" :answer/id #uuid "38120e62-d95b-502d-9288-454ec459aba2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}8y=6 \\\\ 4x+y=-9\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca1fb4a7-0229-50a8-b462-cf1f3e49f409" :answer/id #uuid "ca1fb4a7-0229-50a8-b462-cf1f3e49f409" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}8y=6 \\\\ x+4y=-9\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0af48a4-a01a-5ac1-a551-44dbb13e7334" :answer/id #uuid "b0af48a4-a01a-5ac1-a551-44dbb13e7334" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}8y=6 \\\\ x+4y=9\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57c2694f-57f8-54fb-b264-a6f49a025275" :answer/id #uuid "57c2694f-57f8-54fb-b264-a6f49a025275" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x+8y=6 \\\\ 4x+y=9\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186400387 :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix consists of two parts: the coefficient matrix and the column of constants.\n\nThe coefficient matrix represents the coefficients in the linear system, while the column of constants represents the constants on the right-hand sides of the equations.\n\nUsing the variables $x$, $y$, and $z,$ then, the corresponding system of equations is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}0x-8y+4z=-\\frac{7}{4} \\\\ 0x+5y+\\frac{2}{3}z=8 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}x+\\frac{1}{3}y+4z=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy simplifying, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-8y+4z=-\\frac{7}{4} \\\\ 5y+\\frac{2}{3}z=8 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}x+\\frac{1}{3}y+4z=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186400388 :answer-field/correct "answer-8eff0c23-deb0-5661-9618-e2d13de4135f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a2737fea-cf8b-54fe-91e0-1cf224081a91" "answer-ae1e650f-ec05-53f2-94db-39a6135a9924" "answer-8eff0c23-deb0-5661-9618-e2d13de4135f" "answer-1a9caf8a-d772-5659-bb2a-8be8cd0f8959" "answer-f24f2595-42ba-5741-b8c8-86e447fb2e49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2737fea-cf8b-54fe-91e0-1cf224081a91" :answer/id #uuid "a2737fea-cf8b-54fe-91e0-1cf224081a91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}-8x+4y=-\\frac{7}{4} \\\\ 5x+\\frac{2}{3}y=8 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}x+\\frac{1}{3}y+4z=6\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae1e650f-ec05-53f2-94db-39a6135a9924" :answer/id #uuid "ae1e650f-ec05-53f2-94db-39a6135a9924" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}-8x+4z=-\\frac{7}{4} \\\\ 5x+\\frac{2}{3}z=8 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}x+\\frac{1}{3}y+4z=6\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8eff0c23-deb0-5661-9618-e2d13de4135f" :answer/id #uuid "8eff0c23-deb0-5661-9618-e2d13de4135f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}-8y+4z=-\\frac{7}{4} \\\\ 5y+\\frac{2}{3}z=8 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}x+\\frac{1}{3}y+4z=6\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a9caf8a-d772-5659-bb2a-8be8cd0f8959" :answer/id #uuid "1a9caf8a-d772-5659-bb2a-8be8cd0f8959" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}-8y+4z=\\frac{7}{4} \\\\ 5y+\\frac{2}{3}z=-8 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}x+\\frac{1}{3}y+4z=-6\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f24f2595-42ba-5741-b8c8-86e447fb2e49" :answer/id #uuid "f24f2595-42ba-5741-b8c8-86e447fb2e49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x-8y+4z=-\\frac{7}{4} \\\\ x+5y+\\frac{2}{3}z=8 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}x+\\frac{1}{3}y+4z=6\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186265926 :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}10x+25y=15 \\\\ 12x+3y=-6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=3 \\\\ 4x+y=-2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186265262 :answer-field/correct "answer-727892e1-58ea-5d36-b86b-82b51a10eb55" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a12e8848-d478-59a6-a4bb-c9297a758c18" "answer-1dcde906-c5fb-5fc0-b6a8-8961649a59ba" "answer-b92215d8-8706-55a2-9e83-085b95ecb6b9" "answer-e1575aa2-a070-55bb-b7a7-08d8f4d81a38" "answer-727892e1-58ea-5d36-b86b-82b51a10eb55"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a12e8848-d478-59a6-a4bb-c9297a758c18" :answer/id #uuid "a12e8848-d478-59a6-a4bb-c9297a758c18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}10x+25y=-15 \\\\ 12x+3y=6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1dcde906-c5fb-5fc0-b6a8-8961649a59ba" :answer/id #uuid "1dcde906-c5fb-5fc0-b6a8-8961649a59ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}10x+25y=-15 \\\\ 12x+6y=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b92215d8-8706-55a2-9e83-085b95ecb6b9" :answer/id #uuid "b92215d8-8706-55a2-9e83-085b95ecb6b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}10x+5y=-15 \\\\ 12x+3y=6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1575aa2-a070-55bb-b7a7-08d8f4d81a38" :answer/id #uuid "e1575aa2-a070-55bb-b7a7-08d8f4d81a38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=15 \\\\ 4x+y=-6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-727892e1-58ea-5d36-b86b-82b51a10eb55" :answer/id #uuid "727892e1-58ea-5d36-b86b-82b51a10eb55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=3 \\\\ 4x+y=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186400485 :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}0x+5y=9 \\\\ x+0y=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}5y=9 \\\\ x=-1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186400486 :answer-field/correct "answer-9560da06-25ad-5721-bc24-046715bc8034" :answer-field/choices ["answer-02b3cd2b-284b-5242-a0fd-852bf0b1881c" "answer-9560da06-25ad-5721-bc24-046715bc8034" "answer-2540c038-f7ff-526e-8623-0b2eb9995f47" "answer-86106155-653b-5126-ac12-f97cdb674767" "answer-be15d0f0-70f8-5910-afd6-1af63be69956"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02b3cd2b-284b-5242-a0fd-852bf0b1881c" :answer/id #uuid "02b3cd2b-284b-5242-a0fd-852bf0b1881c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}5y=-9 \\\\ x=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9560da06-25ad-5721-bc24-046715bc8034" :answer/id #uuid "9560da06-25ad-5721-bc24-046715bc8034" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}5y=9 \\\\ x=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2540c038-f7ff-526e-8623-0b2eb9995f47" :answer/id #uuid "2540c038-f7ff-526e-8623-0b2eb9995f47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}5y=9 \\\\ x=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86106155-653b-5126-ac12-f97cdb674767" :answer/id #uuid "86106155-653b-5126-ac12-f97cdb674767" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}x+5y=9 \\\\ x=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be15d0f0-70f8-5910-afd6-1af63be69956" :answer/id #uuid "be15d0f0-70f8-5910-afd6-1af63be69956" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}x+5y=9 \\\\ y=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055047 :question/problem "Let ${S}_{n}=\\{1,2,…,n+1\\},$ where $n\\in N.$ Then, ${S}_{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "To write down the elements of ${S}_{4},$ we substitute $n=4$ into the expression and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{4} & =\\{1,2,…,4+1\\} \\\\  & =\\{1,2,…,5\\} \\\\  & =\\{1,2,3,4,5\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284330 :answer-field/correct "answer-8c60dbcb-cc1b-53d5-9316-a943261ba035" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9441c077-faf1-5bd0-870b-cef8d5a959ed" "answer-8c60dbcb-cc1b-53d5-9316-a943261ba035" "answer-2506c61d-1801-5a64-a80f-0d19c71642d9" "answer-c021623c-4824-596d-bf9c-c8149509df99"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9441c077-faf1-5bd0-870b-cef8d5a959ed" :answer/id #uuid "9441c077-faf1-5bd0-870b-cef8d5a959ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-5,-4,…,4,5\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c60dbcb-cc1b-53d5-9316-a943261ba035" :answer/id #uuid "8c60dbcb-cc1b-53d5-9316-a943261ba035" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{1,2,3,4,5\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2506c61d-1801-5a64-a80f-0d19c71642d9" :answer/id #uuid "2506c61d-1801-5a64-a80f-0d19c71642d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{1,2,3,4\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c021623c-4824-596d-bf9c-c8149509df99" :answer/id #uuid "c021623c-4824-596d-bf9c-c8149509df99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{1,2,…,41\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284704 :question/problem "Let ${D}_{i}=\\{2i-1,-i,1,i+2\\},$ where $i\\in \\{0,2,3,5\\}.$ Then, ${D}_{0}=$" :question/worked-solution "To write down the elements of ${D}_{0},$ we substitute $i=0$ into the expression and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{0} & =\\{2(0)-1,-0,1,0+2\\} \\\\  & =\\{-1,0,1,2\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284282 :answer-field/correct "answer-f276f1af-5dd7-5303-864c-e20940278140" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ae173497-2c5e-5145-a067-5068fba3df55" "answer-f276f1af-5dd7-5303-864c-e20940278140" "answer-8772eabc-6b06-5af0-9a19-b03a8fa68de7" "answer-f4e76a38-ddc0-5fb4-a344-3fc62a1db4b1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae173497-2c5e-5145-a067-5068fba3df55" :answer/id #uuid "ae173497-2c5e-5145-a067-5068fba3df55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-1,0,1,2,3,4,5\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f276f1af-5dd7-5303-864c-e20940278140" :answer/id #uuid "f276f1af-5dd7-5303-864c-e20940278140" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-1,0,1,2\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8772eabc-6b06-5af0-9a19-b03a8fa68de7" :answer/id #uuid "8772eabc-6b06-5af0-9a19-b03a8fa68de7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{0,1,2,3,4,5\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4e76a38-ddc0-5fb4-a344-3fc62a1db4b1" :answer/id #uuid "f4e76a38-ddc0-5fb4-a344-3fc62a1db4b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{0,1,2,3\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284713 :question/problem "Find ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}$, given that $I=\\{0,1,2\\},$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{0}=\\{0\\},\\,{S}_{1}=(0,1),\\,{S}_{2}=(0,2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i} & ={S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2} \\\\  & =\\{0\\}\\,\\cup \\,(0,1)\\,\\cup \\,(0,2) \\\\  & =[0,2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284157 :answer-field/choices ["answer-9f99a0aa-c5bb-5d46-9276-4ffb294c6cb8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f99a0aa-c5bb-5d46-9276-4ffb294c6cb8" :answer/id #uuid "9f99a0aa-c5bb-5d46-9276-4ffb294c6cb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{0,1,2\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284714 :question/problem "Find ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}$, given that $I=\\{5,6,7\\},$ and\n${S}_{i}=[i,\\,i+1).$" :question/worked-solution "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i} & ={S}_{5}\\cup {S}_{6}\\cup {S}_{7} \\\\  & =[5,6)\\,\\cup \\,[6,7)\\,\\cup \\,[7,8) \\\\  & =[5,8).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284313 :answer-field/choices ["answer-d7818a62-4cb5-5eb4-b4b7-350b8c00b6e0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7818a62-4cb5-5eb4-b4b7-350b8c00b6e0" :answer/id #uuid "d7818a62-4cb5-5eb4-b4b7-350b8c00b6e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{5,6,7,8\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284717 :question/problem "Let $I=Z$ and ${X}_{i}=\\{i-1,\\,i\\},$ then ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=$" :question/worked-solution "The intersection of a family of indexed sets $\\{{A}_{i}\\}_{i\\in I}$ contains all elements that belong to *all* sets in our family:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for all }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=-1,$ we have ${X}_{-1}=\\{-2,-1\\}$\n\n- if $i=0,$ we have ${X}_{0}=\\{-1,0\\}$\n\n- if $i=1,$ we have ${X}_{1}=\\{0,1\\}$\n\nand so on. \n\nNotice that there is no element that belongs to all the sets. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284037 :answer-field/choices ["answer-a626081a-f36d-501c-9940-5206c3ddd566" "answer-36833993-965f-54a0-beb6-32d1091dad83" "answer-a516d4ae-3251-52cc-a8ed-64a93fa8df47"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a626081a-f36d-501c-9940-5206c3ddd566" :answer/id #uuid "a626081a-f36d-501c-9940-5206c3ddd566" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{0,\\,1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36833993-965f-54a0-beb6-32d1091dad83" :answer/id #uuid "36833993-965f-54a0-beb6-32d1091dad83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a516d4ae-3251-52cc-a8ed-64a93fa8df47" :answer/id #uuid "a516d4ae-3251-52cc-a8ed-64a93fa8df47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{i\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284719 :question/problem "Let $I=N$ and ${X}_{i}=\\{-i,\\,0,\\,i\\},$ then ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=$" :question/worked-solution "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=1,$ we have ${X}_{1}=\\{-1,0,1\\}$\n\n- if $i=2,$ we have ${X}_{2}=\\{-2,0,2\\}$\n\n- if $i=3,$ we have ${X}_{3}=\\{-3,0,3\\}$\n\nand so on. \n\nNotice that all the integers belong to one of the sets.\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=Z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284197 :answer-field/choices ["answer-9bdaff7d-07de-5c4b-af33-4a521ade7019" "answer-f143606f-f740-553e-8764-98a1d092465f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9bdaff7d-07de-5c4b-af33-4a521ade7019" :answer/id #uuid "9bdaff7d-07de-5c4b-af33-4a521ade7019" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-i,0,i\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f143606f-f740-553e-8764-98a1d092465f" :answer/id #uuid "f143606f-f740-553e-8764-98a1d092465f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186401928 :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=x+2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>x+2.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=-x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge -x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y>x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186401929 :answer-field/correct "answer-4aa2756b-288f-5a3a-97a1-1d111d7e5d71" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4aa2756b-288f-5a3a-97a1-1d111d7e5d71" "answer-740fc491-26cc-5f80-aff8-18126091ad1f" "answer-7aaafe8c-aa58-54f1-83f8-e9d944adc21d" "answer-1db0be1f-16b6-5732-b49d-787adfdfd7fa" "answer-97a3bff2-3169-51e5-adcd-51b59766ae70"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4aa2756b-288f-5a3a-97a1-1d111d7e5d71" :answer/id #uuid "4aa2756b-288f-5a3a-97a1-1d111d7e5d71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y>x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-740fc491-26cc-5f80-aff8-18126091ad1f" :answer/id #uuid "740fc491-26cc-5f80-aff8-18126091ad1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge x+2 \\\\ y<-x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7aaafe8c-aa58-54f1-83f8-e9d944adc21d" :answer/id #uuid "7aaafe8c-aa58-54f1-83f8-e9d944adc21d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1db0be1f-16b6-5732-b49d-787adfdfd7fa" :answer/id #uuid "1db0be1f-16b6-5732-b49d-787adfdfd7fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y<-x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97a3bff2-3169-51e5-adcd-51b59766ae70" :answer/id #uuid "97a3bff2-3169-51e5-adcd-51b59766ae70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y>-x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186302397 :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(-1,3,2)$ and $Q(2,4,5).$ Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ t \\\\ 3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1+3t \\\\ 3+t \\\\ 2+3t\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+3t \\\\ y=3+t \\\\ z=2+3t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186301402 :answer-field/correct "answer-f81bfe5f-a8ad-53cc-9700-e579155f4409" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f81bfe5f-a8ad-53cc-9700-e579155f4409" "answer-483591a0-f429-5fde-9a62-298d56345d72" "answer-93eb3392-70bf-579f-9f36-4778325e3649" "answer-018df1e1-1c2a-53c7-aea3-a1c44c966b71" "answer-efdfe867-7324-58f6-9d1c-0ac24a9c3f9a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f81bfe5f-a8ad-53cc-9700-e579155f4409" :answer/id #uuid "f81bfe5f-a8ad-53cc-9700-e579155f4409" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+3t \\\\ y=3+t \\\\ z=2+3t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-483591a0-f429-5fde-9a62-298d56345d72" :answer/id #uuid "483591a0-f429-5fde-9a62-298d56345d72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-t \\\\ y=3t \\\\ z=2t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93eb3392-70bf-579f-9f36-4778325e3649" :answer/id #uuid "93eb3392-70bf-579f-9f36-4778325e3649" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2-t \\\\ y=4+3t \\\\ z=5+2t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-018df1e1-1c2a-53c7-aea3-a1c44c966b71" :answer/id #uuid "018df1e1-1c2a-53c7-aea3-a1c44c966b71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=3-t \\\\ y=1+3t \\\\ z=3+2t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-efdfe867-7324-58f6-9d1c-0ac24a9c3f9a" :answer/id #uuid "efdfe867-7324-58f6-9d1c-0ac24a9c3f9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=3t \\\\ y=t \\\\ z=3t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186314972 :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=1.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-1=1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=2\\cdot 1=2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186314396 :answer-field/choices ["answer-2efb3d59-10d0-57b0-b6f6-06c1b609ee7f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2efb3d59-10d0-57b0-b6f6-06c1b609ee7f" :answer/id #uuid "2efb3d59-10d0-57b0-b6f6-06c1b609ee7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186317213 :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, ${a}_{3}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=6 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3}=-14 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 6 & -14 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & -14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & -14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=6 \\\\ {x}_{2}=4 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(-2)=6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+4{a}_{2}+(-2){a}_{3} & =b \\\\ 2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+(-2)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=2\\cdot 4\\cdot (-2)=-16.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186316855 :answer-field/choices ["answer-385e50bb-f4df-5245-a484-97539f7d5c09"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-385e50bb-f4df-5245-a484-97539f7d5c09" :answer/id #uuid "385e50bb-f4df-5245-a484-97539f7d5c09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186323896 :question/problem "Which of the following sets is a subset of $A=\\{2n∣n\\in N\\}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must find the elements of the set $A.$ The elements of the set \n$A$ are all the natural even numbers.\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nA=\\{2,4,6,8,…\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, a subset of $A$ is a set whose elements are also elements of the set $A.$\n\nIn our case, $B=\\{2,6,12,14,32\\}$ is a subset of $A.$\n\nIn the rest of the options, the set $B$ has elements that are not in $A,$ meaning that it is not a subset of $A.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186323263 :answer-field/correct "answer-bf4e5029-376f-5549-b5dc-630dc2b81f2a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-056924f8-d83e-5c71-afe8-c472d01bfc53" "answer-03d9004d-0842-578f-917c-13763b0367eb" "answer-6d8f3138-dcd2-5ecb-a537-7faeb8113b84" "answer-9a23dd71-3849-5296-aeae-4e97ffb3e850" "answer-bf4e5029-376f-5549-b5dc-630dc2b81f2a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-056924f8-d83e-5c71-afe8-c472d01bfc53" :answer/id #uuid "056924f8-d83e-5c71-afe8-c472d01bfc53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{-1,0,1,2,4,6\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03d9004d-0842-578f-917c-13763b0367eb" :answer/id #uuid "03d9004d-0842-578f-917c-13763b0367eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{0,1,2,4,6,8\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d8f3138-dcd2-5ecb-a537-7faeb8113b84" :answer/id #uuid "6d8f3138-dcd2-5ecb-a537-7faeb8113b84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{1,3,5,7,9\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a23dd71-3849-5296-aeae-4e97ffb3e850" :answer/id #uuid "9a23dd71-3849-5296-aeae-4e97ffb3e850" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{2,4,6,7\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf4e5029-376f-5549-b5dc-630dc2b81f2a" :answer/id #uuid "bf4e5029-376f-5549-b5dc-630dc2b81f2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{2,6,12,14,32\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186403037 :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=3x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 3x+1.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y\\ge 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186403038 :answer-field/correct "answer-2507c4c0-57e5-598c-863a-a714f06c8cfc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cfc38a19-2695-5509-a01d-a49c31ad8f14" "answer-2507c4c0-57e5-598c-863a-a714f06c8cfc" "answer-9ba1a682-eb65-59eb-ad50-274d91174828" "answer-2e719e7a-6815-5841-a812-f052fcab11b3" "answer-b97e0003-6589-5fcd-8644-42dd6ffff85a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cfc38a19-2695-5509-a01d-a49c31ad8f14" :answer/id #uuid "cfc38a19-2695-5509-a01d-a49c31ad8f14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y<2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2507c4c0-57e5-598c-863a-a714f06c8cfc" :answer/id #uuid "2507c4c0-57e5-598c-863a-a714f06c8cfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y\\ge 2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ba1a682-eb65-59eb-ad50-274d91174828" :answer/id #uuid "9ba1a682-eb65-59eb-ad50-274d91174828" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y\\le 2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e719e7a-6815-5841-a812-f052fcab11b3" :answer/id #uuid "2e719e7a-6815-5841-a812-f052fcab11b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 3x+1 \\\\ y\\ge 2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b97e0003-6589-5fcd-8644-42dd6ffff85a" :answer/id #uuid "b97e0003-6589-5fcd-8644-42dd6ffff85a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 3x+1 \\\\ y\\le 2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186403044 :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=2x+6.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<2x+6.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=5.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y<2x+6 \\\\ y<5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186403045 :answer-field/correct "answer-9185f8e3-ce38-5543-a47b-19be664f85a6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9185f8e3-ce38-5543-a47b-19be664f85a6" "answer-ae8d1241-b069-569c-a2c2-b0ca2c832a9d" "answer-fbefe67e-aa24-5aa2-9d7e-b1ec293ead47" "answer-45bc28e1-f02c-5435-8e27-a7fbd758f3b8" "answer-3c3c859a-fa1e-5f5c-9ccd-c25912b0662c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9185f8e3-ce38-5543-a47b-19be664f85a6" :answer/id #uuid "9185f8e3-ce38-5543-a47b-19be664f85a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y<2x+6 \\\\ y<5\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae8d1241-b069-569c-a2c2-b0ca2c832a9d" :answer/id #uuid "ae8d1241-b069-569c-a2c2-b0ca2c832a9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y<2x+6 \\\\ y>5\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbefe67e-aa24-5aa2-9d7e-b1ec293ead47" :answer/id #uuid "fbefe67e-aa24-5aa2-9d7e-b1ec293ead47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y>2x+6 \\\\ y<5\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45bc28e1-f02c-5435-8e27-a7fbd758f3b8" :answer/id #uuid "45bc28e1-f02c-5435-8e27-a7fbd758f3b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y>2x+6 \\\\ y>5\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c3c859a-fa1e-5f5c-9ccd-c25912b0662c" :answer/id #uuid "3c3c859a-fa1e-5f5c-9ccd-c25912b0662c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 2x+6 \\\\ y\\le 5\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172596 :question/problem "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{1})=[]+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{1})\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{1}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $3$ and position $1$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe location of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{1})$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{1}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{2}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{3}) \\\\  &  &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{1})$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So,\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{1})=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{0})+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{1})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{0}).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186335310 :answer-field/correct "answer-80b40976-92df-5d2c-86ee-4dc5ee7ca40b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9a7a61d3-30ae-5e41-aea0-85e5dcd146d4" "answer-78ddad5a-92bc-5076-b3a4-c6e43df1cb7e" "answer-80b40976-92df-5d2c-86ee-4dc5ee7ca40b" "answer-805f4e52-0148-5922-8396-e0236216c0d8" "answer-e61bdf0f-ed23-51fc-a2c4-a20c5b93a968"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a7a61d3-30ae-5e41-aea0-85e5dcd146d4" :answer/id #uuid "9a7a61d3-30ae-5e41-aea0-85e5dcd146d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{1}{0})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78ddad5a-92bc-5076-b3a4-c6e43df1cb7e" :answer/id #uuid "78ddad5a-92bc-5076-b3a4-c6e43df1cb7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{1}{1})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80b40976-92df-5d2c-86ee-4dc5ee7ca40b" :answer/id #uuid "80b40976-92df-5d2c-86ee-4dc5ee7ca40b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{0})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-805f4e52-0148-5922-8396-e0236216c0d8" :answer/id #uuid "805f4e52-0148-5922-8396-e0236216c0d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{1})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e61bdf0f-ed23-51fc-a2c4-a20c5b93a968" :answer/id #uuid "e61bdf0f-ed23-51fc-a2c4-a20c5b93a968" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186335995 :question/problem "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{2})=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{1})+[]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{2}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $3$ and position $2$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe location of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{2})$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{1}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{2}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{3}) \\\\  &  &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{2})$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So,\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{2})=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{1})+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{2})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{2}).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186335645 :answer-field/correct "answer-4f61bb02-7c6b-599e-bcda-28faca2378f8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7b20281e-3116-5c7a-9362-f88b58a1e766" "answer-3d54b2a8-70b8-57d2-b26c-e1b263ac6824" "answer-809103a8-aba5-597f-b3d9-d4ff88026e05" "answer-a725e35f-5fa7-5d30-a593-8ae1d44e2785" "answer-4f61bb02-7c6b-599e-bcda-28faca2378f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b20281e-3116-5c7a-9362-f88b58a1e766" :answer/id #uuid "7b20281e-3116-5c7a-9362-f88b58a1e766" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{1}{0})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d54b2a8-70b8-57d2-b26c-e1b263ac6824" :answer/id #uuid "3d54b2a8-70b8-57d2-b26c-e1b263ac6824" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{1}{1})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-809103a8-aba5-597f-b3d9-d4ff88026e05" :answer/id #uuid "809103a8-aba5-597f-b3d9-d4ff88026e05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{0})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a725e35f-5fa7-5d30-a593-8ae1d44e2785" :answer/id #uuid "a725e35f-5fa7-5d30-a593-8ae1d44e2785" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{1})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f61bb02-7c6b-599e-bcda-28faca2378f8" :answer/id #uuid "4f61bb02-7c6b-599e-bcda-28faca2378f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186338838 :question/worked-solution "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nComparing the above to our given equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-11}{-4}=\\frac{y-(-3)}{5}=\\frac{z-(-1)}{3},\n$$\n\nwe find that our line passes through the point $P(11,-3,-1)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨-4,5,3⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations are the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=11-4t \\\\ y=-3+5t \\\\ z=-1+3t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186338687 :answer-field/correct "answer-4b7409a3-17df-5f35-9a98-53b2b56e27b0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2aad0314-cdde-56d6-9fc9-f1e44fdcf531" "answer-2670e300-5558-54cf-aa24-1fbeb9d684b0" "answer-b720935d-3a6b-53b7-8467-e0328c75249f" "answer-4b7409a3-17df-5f35-9a98-53b2b56e27b0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2aad0314-cdde-56d6-9fc9-f1e44fdcf531" :answer/id #uuid "2aad0314-cdde-56d6-9fc9-f1e44fdcf531" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-11-4t \\\\ y=3+5t \\\\ z=1+3t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2670e300-5558-54cf-aa24-1fbeb9d684b0" :answer/id #uuid "2670e300-5558-54cf-aa24-1fbeb9d684b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-4+11t \\\\ y=5-3t \\\\ z=3-t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b720935d-3a6b-53b7-8467-e0328c75249f" :answer/id #uuid "b720935d-3a6b-53b7-8467-e0328c75249f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-4t \\\\ y=5t \\\\ z=3t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b7409a3-17df-5f35-9a98-53b2b56e27b0" :answer/id #uuid "4b7409a3-17df-5f35-9a98-53b2b56e27b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=11-4t \\\\ y=-3+5t \\\\ z=-1+3t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186351158 :question/problem "Find all of the subsets of $U=\\{-\\pi ,\\pi \\}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find every subset of $U,$ we list out every combination of elements within $U.$ \n\nWe can use the following diagram to visualize the process:\n\n![](images/b0/b0e483a2d10cba17fb2bd3bf0e78d7b4d2fc07b22dbb5c492564b998bbfce6fc.png)\n\nNote that we must include the empty set since it is a subset of every set.\n\nBy doing this, we get\n\n$$\n∅,\\{-\\pi \\},\\{\\pi \\},\\{-\\pi ,\\pi \\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186351128 :answer-field/correct "answer-a581296f-1ffd-5680-83b4-0a132fb259d4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cceb7cd8-d3cb-5022-80c1-91cc18c492dd" "answer-a7e833ed-7b92-5b0e-ac1a-b54703f7a2bf" "answer-d6a266a0-5552-509f-ae6b-32ef2b01771f" "answer-8560767a-af4e-5ac9-984b-0d56ecc22cf9" "answer-a581296f-1ffd-5680-83b4-0a132fb259d4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cceb7cd8-d3cb-5022-80c1-91cc18c492dd" :answer/id #uuid "cceb7cd8-d3cb-5022-80c1-91cc18c492dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-\\pi \\},\\{\\pi \\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7e833ed-7b92-5b0e-ac1a-b54703f7a2bf" :answer/id #uuid "a7e833ed-7b92-5b0e-ac1a-b54703f7a2bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-\\pi \\},\\{\\pi \\},\\{-\\pi ,\\pi \\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6a266a0-5552-509f-ae6b-32ef2b01771f" :answer/id #uuid "d6a266a0-5552-509f-ae6b-32ef2b01771f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅,\\{-\\pi ,\\pi \\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8560767a-af4e-5ac9-984b-0d56ecc22cf9" :answer/id #uuid "8560767a-af4e-5ac9-984b-0d56ecc22cf9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅,\\{-\\pi \\},\\{\\pi \\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a581296f-1ffd-5680-83b4-0a132fb259d4" :answer/id #uuid "a581296f-1ffd-5680-83b4-0a132fb259d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅,\\{-\\pi \\},\\{\\pi \\},\\{-\\pi ,\\pi \\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186351176 :question/worked-solution "The multiples of $10$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nC=\\{10,20,30,40,50,60,70,…\\}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $5$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nD=\\{5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,45,50,55,60,65,70,75,…\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, $C∖D$ is the *difference* of $C$ and $D,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $C$ but *not* in $D.$\n\nThe elements of $C$ that are also in $D$ are $10,20,30,40,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $10$). So, we must remove these elements from $C.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C∖D & =C-D \\\\  & =\\{10,20,30,40,50,60,70,…\\}-\\{5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,45,50,55,60,65,70,75,…\\} \\\\  & =∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186351004 :answer-field/choices ["answer-1eee49b7-7d23-57d3-be48-80546786725e" "answer-d54904e8-c3f4-50ab-b94b-312c9c80dbb1" "answer-3656c7be-564a-5dca-b523-f1cf8ca9939f" "answer-e8c1a6ce-e81b-50b5-825e-bab71ce12858"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1eee49b7-7d23-57d3-be48-80546786725e" :answer/id #uuid "1eee49b7-7d23-57d3-be48-80546786725e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{10,20,30,40,50,60,70,…\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d54904e8-c3f4-50ab-b94b-312c9c80dbb1" :answer/id #uuid "d54904e8-c3f4-50ab-b94b-312c9c80dbb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{15,30,45,60,75,…\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3656c7be-564a-5dca-b523-f1cf8ca9939f" :answer/id #uuid "3656c7be-564a-5dca-b523-f1cf8ca9939f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,45,50,55,60,65,70,75,…\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8c1a6ce-e81b-50b5-825e-bab71ce12858" :answer/id #uuid "e8c1a6ce-e81b-50b5-825e-bab71ce12858" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{5,15,25,35,45,55,65,75,…\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186351258 :question/problem "If $U=\\{1,2,3,…,10\\}$ is the universal set and $A=\\{2,4,6,8,10\\},$ then the complement of $A$ is" :question/worked-solution "The complement of $A,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{A},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $A.$\n\nThe elements of $U$ that are not in $A$ are $1,$ $3,$ $5,$ $7,$ and $9.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{A}=\\{1,3,5,7,9\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186350765 :answer-field/correct "answer-32175474-2a33-5edd-82d1-ca23fe06b582" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8e2a7810-134a-59c6-95e0-9e32883d711d" "answer-5b05c18c-16d7-52fb-815b-13f340ae470d" "answer-32175474-2a33-5edd-82d1-ca23fe06b582" "answer-0ae8da4d-49d1-5d59-b5f2-9ba7fac1a5ce" "answer-62686a45-f9e0-5352-8bd0-280e32a4a7dd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e2a7810-134a-59c6-95e0-9e32883d711d" :answer/id #uuid "8e2a7810-134a-59c6-95e0-9e32883d711d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{0,3,6,9\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b05c18c-16d7-52fb-815b-13f340ae470d" :answer/id #uuid "5b05c18c-16d7-52fb-815b-13f340ae470d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-32175474-2a33-5edd-82d1-ca23fe06b582" :answer/id #uuid "32175474-2a33-5edd-82d1-ca23fe06b582" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{1,3,5,7,9\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ae8da4d-49d1-5d59-b5f2-9ba7fac1a5ce" :answer/id #uuid "0ae8da4d-49d1-5d59-b5f2-9ba7fac1a5ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{1,3,6,9\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62686a45-f9e0-5352-8bd0-280e32a4a7dd" :answer/id #uuid "62686a45-f9e0-5352-8bd0-280e32a4a7dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{3,5,7,9\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186351259 :question/problem "If $U=\\{-20,-18,-16,-14,…,20\\}$ is the universal set and $A=\\{-20,-16,-12,-8,…,20\\},$ then $\\overset{―}{A}=$" :question/worked-solution "The complement of $A,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{A},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $A.$\n\nThe universal set $U$ consists of the even integers $-20$ through $20,$ while the set $A$ consists of the multiples of $4$ from $-20$ through $20.$\n\nSo, the only elements of $U$ that are not in $A$ are the even integers from $-18$ through $18$ that are not multiples of $4.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{A}=\\{-18,-14,-10,-6,-2,2,6,10,14,18\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186350983 :answer-field/correct "answer-16477003-cf0b-5c83-86c6-010a4fd01ccd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1f9b53a9-1ace-522a-a982-9f2273e85246" "answer-aca7987c-36a3-5372-90f4-1bc62f2eb30e" "answer-16477003-cf0b-5c83-86c6-010a4fd01ccd" "answer-3943ae65-9d1c-52ad-ac6f-f19c4854ec2a" "answer-92200749-20dc-58fb-8a4b-402b623d1530"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f9b53a9-1ace-522a-a982-9f2273e85246" :answer/id #uuid "1f9b53a9-1ace-522a-a982-9f2273e85246" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-16,-14,-12,-10,…,16\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aca7987c-36a3-5372-90f4-1bc62f2eb30e" :answer/id #uuid "aca7987c-36a3-5372-90f4-1bc62f2eb30e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-18,-12,-6,0,6,12,18\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16477003-cf0b-5c83-86c6-010a4fd01ccd" :answer/id #uuid "16477003-cf0b-5c83-86c6-010a4fd01ccd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-18,-14,-10,-6,-2,2,6,10,14,18\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3943ae65-9d1c-52ad-ac6f-f19c4854ec2a" :answer/id #uuid "3943ae65-9d1c-52ad-ac6f-f19c4854ec2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-18,-16,-14,-12,…,18\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92200749-20dc-58fb-8a4b-402b623d1530" :answer/id #uuid "92200749-20dc-58fb-8a4b-402b623d1530" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-20,-16,-12,-8,-4,0,4,8,12,16\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186351347 :question/problem "![](images/3b/3b539190899ca580528fdbf7b5d3ef9925ade29f97f4b2f96b0f1394743f40a8.png)\n\nGiven the sets $S=\\{p,a,s,w,o,r,d\\}$ and $T=\\{p,o,r,t,e,l\\},$ find $T∖S.$" :question/worked-solution "The difference $T∖S$ consists of all the elements that are in $T$ but not $S.$ To represent $T∖S,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $T$ but not $S.$\n\n![](images/c7/c718918667c5076f8696ea98f453ff17f005d5f7cace87bd863be309fac28d72.png)\n\nThe elements $t,e,$ and $l$ are in $T$ but not $S.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nT∖S=\\{t,e,l\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186350742 :answer-field/correct "answer-cde8a77d-917c-5d32-aebb-5d7a0c324a5d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-44d69e04-701b-532a-8660-e10b61e27da0" "answer-c0ebd0cd-50f3-5d9b-b33d-13fa3b3356f9" "answer-6386c1eb-6556-5007-86bd-5b23aac19731" "answer-3e57db84-9532-5a86-b209-39f3021ccc79" "answer-cde8a77d-917c-5d32-aebb-5d7a0c324a5d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44d69e04-701b-532a-8660-e10b61e27da0" :answer/id #uuid "44d69e04-701b-532a-8660-e10b61e27da0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{a,s,w,d\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0ebd0cd-50f3-5d9b-b33d-13fa3b3356f9" :answer/id #uuid "c0ebd0cd-50f3-5d9b-b33d-13fa3b3356f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{p,a,s,t,e,l\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6386c1eb-6556-5007-86bd-5b23aac19731" :answer/id #uuid "6386c1eb-6556-5007-86bd-5b23aac19731" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{p,o,r\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e57db84-9532-5a86-b209-39f3021ccc79" :answer/id #uuid "3e57db84-9532-5a86-b209-39f3021ccc79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{t,e,l,a,s,w,d\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cde8a77d-917c-5d32-aebb-5d7a0c324a5d" :answer/id #uuid "cde8a77d-917c-5d32-aebb-5d7a0c324a5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{t,e,l\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186351367 :question/worked-solution "The multiples of $3$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA=\\{3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24,…\\}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB=\\{4,8,12,16,20,24,…\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, $B-A$ is the *difference* of $B$ and $A,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $B$ but *not* in $A.$\n\nThe elements of $B$ that are also in $A$ are $12,24,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $12$). So, we must remove these elements from $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-A & =\\{4,8,12,16,20,24,…\\}-\\{3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24,…\\} \\\\  & =\\{4,8,16,20,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186350721 :answer-field/correct "answer-b6cb932c-85b3-56d0-b40c-f7eaaf738441" :answer-field/choices ["answer-59d2bdb8-067c-5558-99a7-7af0349458cd" "answer-8ad10406-2414-5636-81d1-8eab697da0a6" "answer-3caf765e-af4f-5636-a6be-d1ba59a6b778" "answer-469ad4f5-346a-5a0c-a575-a0d28114f6c9" "answer-b6cb932c-85b3-56d0-b40c-f7eaaf738441"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59d2bdb8-067c-5558-99a7-7af0349458cd" :answer/id #uuid "59d2bdb8-067c-5558-99a7-7af0349458cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{0,3,6,9,15,18,21,…\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ad10406-2414-5636-81d1-8eab697da0a6" :answer/id #uuid "8ad10406-2414-5636-81d1-8eab697da0a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{12,24…\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3caf765e-af4f-5636-a6be-d1ba59a6b778" :answer/id #uuid "3caf765e-af4f-5636-a6be-d1ba59a6b778" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{3,4,6,8,9,15,16,…\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-469ad4f5-346a-5a0c-a575-a0d28114f6c9" :answer/id #uuid "469ad4f5-346a-5a0c-a575-a0d28114f6c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{3,6,9,15,18,21,…\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6cb932c-85b3-56d0-b40c-f7eaaf738441" :answer/id #uuid "b6cb932c-85b3-56d0-b40c-f7eaaf738441" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{4,8,16,20,…\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186354480 :question/problem "![](images/02/02dabe7099c201f717885a05842e0cb8543bd01cccf0d6c52147f674cde15dce.png)\n\nLet $U=\\{a,b,c,20,40\\}$ be the universal set and let $R=\\{b,20,40\\}.$ What is the complement of $R?$" :question/worked-solution "The complement of $R,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{R},$ consists of all the elements in $U$ that are not in $R.$ To represent $\\overset{―}{R},$ we will shade in all the area of $U$ that is *outside* of $R,$ as follows:\n\n![](images/79/79900f22c35570b35cf10664768ecf4460a7953ddf7f91dac1893b3ce81339bf.png)\n\nThe elements in the shaded area are $a$ and $c.$ These are the elements of $U$ that are not in $R.$ Therefore, the complement of $R$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{R}=\\{a,c\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186353842 :answer-field/correct "answer-5295dfc9-a8d9-5012-aa1a-6489385fb437" :answer-field/choices ["answer-81c96ee9-b80c-53be-8db0-4ae74de56f46" "answer-6aa239f7-6bc9-5d19-a04a-3903bf7b1d89" "answer-22020fe8-3d17-509a-ba0b-2431b2f443de" "answer-5295dfc9-a8d9-5012-aa1a-6489385fb437" "answer-da7a201d-4e4b-50a4-a478-467f445ad325"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81c96ee9-b80c-53be-8db0-4ae74de56f46" :answer/id #uuid "81c96ee9-b80c-53be-8db0-4ae74de56f46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{20,40\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6aa239f7-6bc9-5d19-a04a-3903bf7b1d89" :answer/id #uuid "6aa239f7-6bc9-5d19-a04a-3903bf7b1d89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{a,40\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22020fe8-3d17-509a-ba0b-2431b2f443de" :answer/id #uuid "22020fe8-3d17-509a-ba0b-2431b2f443de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{a,b,c\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5295dfc9-a8d9-5012-aa1a-6489385fb437" :answer/id #uuid "5295dfc9-a8d9-5012-aa1a-6489385fb437" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{a,c\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da7a201d-4e4b-50a4-a478-467f445ad325" :answer/id #uuid "da7a201d-4e4b-50a4-a478-467f445ad325" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{c,40\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186354481 :question/problem "If $U=\\{2,4,6,8,10,12\\}$ is the universal set and $B=\\{2,6,10\\},$ then the complement of $B$ is" :question/worked-solution "The complement of $B,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{B},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $B.$\n\nThe elements of $U$ that are not in $B$ are $4,$ $8,$   and $12.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $B$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{B}=\\{4,8,12\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186354100 :answer-field/correct "answer-35957b83-2a68-58c6-869c-f6146120f1db" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4e158fb2-27a7-51b7-ac36-dee0da33f3b4" "answer-670ae3f8-93f9-5d03-9ecb-0dfcaa09ffbe" "answer-49084c79-d854-50d1-b930-1bc749d78ada" "answer-35957b83-2a68-58c6-869c-f6146120f1db" "answer-71202aab-95d1-5922-b4cf-8610084c1a4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e158fb2-27a7-51b7-ac36-dee0da33f3b4" :answer/id #uuid "4e158fb2-27a7-51b7-ac36-dee0da33f3b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{2,4,8,12\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-670ae3f8-93f9-5d03-9ecb-0dfcaa09ffbe" :answer/id #uuid "670ae3f8-93f9-5d03-9ecb-0dfcaa09ffbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{4,12\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49084c79-d854-50d1-b930-1bc749d78ada" :answer/id #uuid "49084c79-d854-50d1-b930-1bc749d78ada" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{4,8,10,12\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35957b83-2a68-58c6-869c-f6146120f1db" :answer/id #uuid "35957b83-2a68-58c6-869c-f6146120f1db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{4,8,12\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71202aab-95d1-5922-b4cf-8610084c1a4c" :answer/id #uuid "71202aab-95d1-5922-b4cf-8610084c1a4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{4,8\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186354497 :question/problem "![](images/96/96962d11526f30beee45b85aac92808518352d7b79b4b4f2e4a7351ddd9fe17e.png)\n\nGiven the sets $S=\\{5,7,9\\}$ and $T=\\{0,1,3\\},$find $S∖T.$" :question/worked-solution "The difference $S∖T$ consists of all the elements that are in $S$ but not $T.$ To represent $S∖T,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $S$ but not $T.$\n\n![](images/be/be1caefc99bea5d4dde0ba272a208dd8f587156029ce37df483e40cd5f6121d2.png)\n\nAll elements of $S$ are not in $T.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nS∖T=\\{5,7,9\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186354073 :answer-field/correct "answer-c624021e-1fb1-5744-8539-f9b2fa9ef8eb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1a0f4d4a-32b2-546c-9f78-4d850b9be5a7" "answer-774c28d2-891a-5484-8cb3-157bc707a2b6" "answer-c624021e-1fb1-5744-8539-f9b2fa9ef8eb" "answer-62474c25-a7fa-510e-996c-b49c4b498820"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a0f4d4a-32b2-546c-9f78-4d850b9be5a7" :answer/id #uuid "1a0f4d4a-32b2-546c-9f78-4d850b9be5a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{0,1,3,5,7,9\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-774c28d2-891a-5484-8cb3-157bc707a2b6" :answer/id #uuid "774c28d2-891a-5484-8cb3-157bc707a2b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{0,1,3\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c624021e-1fb1-5744-8539-f9b2fa9ef8eb" :answer/id #uuid "c624021e-1fb1-5744-8539-f9b2fa9ef8eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{5,7,9\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62474c25-a7fa-510e-996c-b49c4b498820" :answer/id #uuid "62474c25-a7fa-510e-996c-b49c4b498820" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{5,7\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186404461 :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $x+y=3.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=-x+3.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\"  inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>-x+3,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx+y>3.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y=2x.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict.  Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>2x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y>3 \\\\ y>2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186404462 :answer-field/correct "answer-27635777-a8dd-5afe-a296-ee402af7fe39" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7fa72215-7cb2-51f3-b5db-2adac83c439f" "answer-6f580ecb-7efc-5512-9398-273631dd1bd9" "answer-480417bf-3b78-555e-8194-c8ef38995e34" "answer-27635777-a8dd-5afe-a296-ee402af7fe39" "answer-b0260bc6-012f-5b9c-a80e-93287d27b6c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7fa72215-7cb2-51f3-b5db-2adac83c439f" :answer/id #uuid "7fa72215-7cb2-51f3-b5db-2adac83c439f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y<3 \\\\ y<2x\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f580ecb-7efc-5512-9398-273631dd1bd9" :answer/id #uuid "6f580ecb-7efc-5512-9398-273631dd1bd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y<3 \\\\ y>2x\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-480417bf-3b78-555e-8194-c8ef38995e34" :answer/id #uuid "480417bf-3b78-555e-8194-c8ef38995e34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y>3 \\\\ y<2x\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27635777-a8dd-5afe-a296-ee402af7fe39" :answer/id #uuid "27635777-a8dd-5afe-a296-ee402af7fe39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y>3 \\\\ y>2x\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0260bc6-012f-5b9c-a80e-93287d27b6c3" :answer/id #uuid "b0260bc6-012f-5b9c-a80e-93287d27b6c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y\\le 3 \\\\ y\\ge 2x\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186404468 :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=4x+3.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<4x+3.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{4}x-2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>\\frac{1}{4}x-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y<4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186404469 :answer-field/correct "answer-fbeae658-1ad6-5399-b8e3-d95d56f3c62b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fbeae658-1ad6-5399-b8e3-d95d56f3c62b" "answer-8ff44b6f-7f18-5b59-b687-6bfafa9923c1" "answer-c6b98254-dc2c-5569-ba7c-775a46563922" "answer-21f1cf91-2163-5bf5-8bdd-17c06cfb56f3" "answer-49247309-afac-5793-a965-e29d26e684cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbeae658-1ad6-5399-b8e3-d95d56f3c62b" :answer/id #uuid "fbeae658-1ad6-5399-b8e3-d95d56f3c62b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y<4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ff44b6f-7f18-5b59-b687-6bfafa9923c1" :answer/id #uuid "8ff44b6f-7f18-5b59-b687-6bfafa9923c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y>4x+3 \\\\ y<\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6b98254-dc2c-5569-ba7c-775a46563922" :answer/id #uuid "c6b98254-dc2c-5569-ba7c-775a46563922" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y>4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21f1cf91-2163-5bf5-8bdd-17c06cfb56f3" :answer/id #uuid "21f1cf91-2163-5bf5-8bdd-17c06cfb56f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y>4x+3 \\\\ y\\ge \\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49247309-afac-5793-a965-e29d26e684cb" :answer/id #uuid "49247309-afac-5793-a965-e29d26e684cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186404475 :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=x+2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le x+2.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=-x+2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>-x+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y>-x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186404476 :answer-field/correct "answer-ea85fa77-5fe3-59b1-a642-7a3377ab8ed7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a6ae492d-6998-592e-aad4-9e4158c3d62a" "answer-8760f28c-314a-5353-a151-1773d06194c2" "answer-d086efec-878a-5d60-959f-69c0d1d6a64c" "answer-ea85fa77-5fe3-59b1-a642-7a3377ab8ed7" "answer-dfc950a4-a4b3-574a-9a32-22ca9de0541d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6ae492d-6998-592e-aad4-9e4158c3d62a" :answer/id #uuid "a6ae492d-6998-592e-aad4-9e4158c3d62a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y<x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8760f28c-314a-5353-a151-1773d06194c2" :answer/id #uuid "8760f28c-314a-5353-a151-1773d06194c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y>x+2 \\\\ y\\le -x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d086efec-878a-5d60-959f-69c0d1d6a64c" :answer/id #uuid "d086efec-878a-5d60-959f-69c0d1d6a64c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge x+2 \\\\ y<-x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea85fa77-5fe3-59b1-a642-7a3377ab8ed7" :answer/id #uuid "ea85fa77-5fe3-59b1-a642-7a3377ab8ed7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y>-x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfc950a4-a4b3-574a-9a32-22ca9de0541d" :answer/id #uuid "dfc950a4-a4b3-574a-9a32-22ca9de0541d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}]
